{"ts": "2026-06-08T05:56:06.130Z", "level": "INFO", "logger": "infereval.endorsement", "event": "sample.completed", "item_id": "row-1", "sample_index": 1, "provider": "anthropic", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "request_id": "retest-auto-02f7a2c5-0:row-1:sample-1", "prompt_hash": "sha256:cbfadf19184447bfc004bbca5412f6db4276bc8be1f186b0b5c1d44b1cb3d8fe", "raw_response": "BAD\n\nThe premise that \"it is nighttime\" is a defeater for the conclusion that the stop sign \"visibly appears red.\" At night, without adequate lighting, a stop sign would not visibly appear red—it would appear dark or black, or be visible only if illuminated by headlights or other light sources. The nighttime condition contradicts the ordinary conditions under which a stop sign would visibly appear red.", "parsed_verdict": "bad", "parse_status": "ok", "wall_time_ms": 1392.5978330080397, "input_tokens": 258, "output_tokens": 92, "finish_reason": "end_turn", "reasoning_tokens": null, "benchmark_id": "stop-sign-perceptual", "framework_version": "0.15.2", "run_id": "retest-auto-02f7a2c5-0"}
